Title:
EVENSTAR — Intel 64 / Windows Low-Level Experiments

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- EVENSTAR is a collection of Intel x64 Windows low-level experiments and proof-of-concepts focused on kernel/user internals, debugging, and telemetry.  
- The repo includes multiple small projects such as ETW consumers (syscall, Threat Intelligence, and Kernel Audit API calls), kernel write-protection experiments, and kernel-to-user injection research.  
- It explores how Windows exposes (and can be made to expose) execution and security-relevant signals via ETW, and how those signals may be evaded or altered from kernel context.  
- Several components are oriented around introspection/debugging (e.g., reading IDT/KDBG data, paging-related debugger extensions) and CPU/processor-mode detection.  
- Useful for red teamers and security researchers studying EDR/ETW visibility boundaries, as well as blue teamers validating what telemetry is available and how it can be bypassed.  
- Interesting because it consolidates practical, code-level experiments around ETW sensors and kernel memory protections, which are common choke points for modern detection.

Technical Focus:
- ETW consumers (Syscall, Threat Intelligence, Kernel Audit API Calls)
- Kernel-to-user injection techniques
- Kernel write protection / memory manipulation (e.g., PFN remapping)
- Windows kernel debugging extensions (IDT/KDBG/paging introspection)
- CPU/processor mode and processor-number detection on Windows x64

Use Cases:
- Build lab tooling to consume and analyze ETW syscall/TI/audit streams
- Research ETW-based detection coverage and potential evasion strategies
- Prototype kernel-assisted injection and study userland visibility artifacts
- Experiment with kernel memory write-protection bypass/alteration techniques
- Develop WinDbg/DbgEng extensions for kernel structure and paging analysis

Keywords:
Windows x64, Intel 64, ETW, Event Tracing for Windows, Syscall tracing, ETW Threat Intelligence, Kernel Audit API Calls, EDR telemetry, kernel-mode, user-mode, kernel-to-user injection, kernel memory, write protection, PFN remapping, paging, IDT, KDBG, WinDbg extension, Windows internals